                                                            <comment id="106176" author="712020:ed93635f-fc45-4097-b174-29a6977381a3" created="Mon, 10 Nov 2025 11:45:55 -0500"  >&lt;p&gt;Just got access and it looks like it is Simplify Fusebox.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;/rest/api/3/attachment/content/42989&quot; alt=&quot;image-20251110-164507.png&quot; width=&quot;812&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                                                            <comment id="106182" author="712020:28b1e0c6-06c6-4e94-ba4f-35afe4004c3a" created="Mon, 10 Nov 2025 14:01:24 -0500"  >&lt;p&gt;Dev Note: These are the apparent requirements to reproduce this:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Payment Processor must be Simplify Fusebox&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Multiple credit cards used on the same SALE transaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;At this time I&#8217;m not sure if the issue is that our front end POS is populating a the TransComment field with this data; we&#8217;ll have to take a look.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                                                            <comment id="106937" author="712020:eaf727a0-f2d0-4fb8-ae93-c46f277555b6" created="Wed, 19 Nov 2025 17:10:31 -0500"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://qcmigration.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A28b1e0c6-06c6-4e94-ba4f-35afe4004c3a&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;712020:28b1e0c6-06c6-4e94-ba4f-35afe4004c3a&quot; data-account-id=&quot;712020:28b1e0c6-06c6-4e94-ba4f-35afe4004c3a&quot; accountid=&quot;712020:28b1e0c6-06c6-4e94-ba4f-35afe4004c3a&quot; rel=&quot;noreferrer&quot;&gt;Eric Lundin&lt;/a&gt;  I found a code snippet where add Credit Card information to the comment. It appears to be in a &#8220;void&#8221; section however I am wondering if the split transaction could have led to this logic.&lt;/p&gt;

